questions.question:
Fill in the blanks — which decorator must be outermost (top) so that an abstract static method is created correctly? Why is the opposite order illegal?
```python
from abc import ABC, abstractmethod

class S(ABC):
    @____        # blank 1
    @____        # blank 2
    def make(self):
        ...
```

questions.answer:
Blank 1 (outermost) = staticmethod; blank 2 (innermost) = abstractmethod. The order matters because abstractmethod sets a flag, and staticmethod must wrap the flagged function.

code:
from abc import ABC, abstractmethod

class S(ABC):
    @staticmethod
    @abstractmethod
    def make(self):
        ...

real example:
Reversing the two decorators raises AttributeError because staticmethod objects reject the flag write.

